   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to excluding certain lottery\nwinnings from a school district's adjusted gross income",
    "basePrintNo": "S8701",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8701-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 57,
       "fullName": "George Borrello",
       "imgName": "57_george_borrello.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1370,
       "sessionMemberId": 1800,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "BORRELLO"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3602, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8701\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to excluding certain\nlottery winnings from a school district's adjusted gross income\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to prevent lottery winnings from having a\nnegative impact on state aid to school districts.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections 1 and 2 modify section 3602 of the Education Law by adding a\nsentence to the definition of \"adjusted gross income\" indicating that\nany lottery winnings in excess of twenty-five percent of a district's\nadjusted gross income shall be excluded from such district's adjusted\ngross income for the year.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMuch of the aid that school districts receive from the state is known as\n\"formula-based aid.\" The formula uses a variety of factors, including\nthe district's adjusted gross income, to determine the district's need.\nWhen a resident of a given district wins the lottery, this increases the\ndistrict's adjusted gross income, and in turn, reduces their perceived\nneed and the amount of aid they will receive.\n\nIn order to prevent lottery winnings from having a negative impact on\nschool budgets, this bill requires that any lottery winnings that add up\nto a quarter or more of a district's adjusted gross income not be\nfactored into the aid formula.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nWill enable school districts to maintain adequate funding.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
